Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** of your integration test suite.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| **High** | 3 | 3 |
| **Medium** | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

All 19 catalog smells were checked. 15 smells were **not detected**. The remaining 4 tests (`InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`, `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`, `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`, `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`) are affected. The other 4 tests are clean.

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // blocks for 3 seconds
```

**Why it's still High despite `[TestCategory("Integration")]`:** Per calibration rules, Sleepy Test severity is *not* downgraded for integration tests — arbitrary sleeps cause flakiness and slow suites at any scope. Additionally, this method is `async Task` yet uses a synchronous `Thread.Sleep`, blocking the thread pool.

**Concrete fix — poll with a timeout:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll until the notification arrives (up to 5 s)
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
    while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id)
           && DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        "Notification was not sent within the expected time window.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** 3-second floor on every run; false failures when the system is slightly slower than 3 s; false passes when it takes slightly longer.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

The `if/else` means **one branch never executes** — the test silently skips half its logic every run. Because the insert creates a plain `User`, the `PremiumUser` branch is dead code that gives false confidence in `DiscountRate` coverage.

**Concrete fix — write two explicit tests:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vip", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0,
        "Premium users must have a positive discount rate.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** `PremiumUser.DiscountRate` is never actually tested; regression can ship unnoticed.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion
}
```

The method name suggests a "does not throw" intent, which is acknowledged — but MSTest reports this as **passed** even if `Insert` silently discards every row. Without an assertion, this test provides zero regression safety.

**Concrete fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count, "All 100 bulk-inserted users should be persisted.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Silent data-loss bugs pass the suite; false confidence in bulk-insert codepath.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

Four assertions, **zero explanation messages**. When one fails in CI, the log shows only `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<…>` with no context about *which* property or *why* this matters.

**Concrete fix — add message parameters:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name must round-trip through the database.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email must round-trip through the database.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Database should assign a positive auto-increment ID.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower failure diagnosis in CI; developers re-run locally instead of reading the log.

---

## Smells NOT Detected (15 of 19 — Clean)

| Smell | Status | Note |
|-------|--------|------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite is hermetic; `[TestCategory("Integration")]` acknowledged |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | No test calls 4+ distinct production methods; integration scope applies |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | `3` and `10` in count assertions are contextually obvious (items just added) |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `.ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test method |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` or skipped tests |
| Assertion Roulette | Partial | Only 1 method exceeds the 3+ threshold |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No identical assertion pairs |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Each test exercises a distinct behavior |
| Constructor Init | ✅ Clean | Uses `[TestInitialize]` correctly |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Class name is meaningful |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No debug output statements |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | In-memory DB, no assumed external files |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | All methods have executable statements |

## Well-Written Tests (Smell-Free)

These 4 tests are solid and can serve as templates:

- **`UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord`** — clear arrange/act/assert, focused scope
- **`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`** — clean negative check with `Assert.IsNull`
- **`ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`** — good use of `CollectionAssert`, contextual count
- **`InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity`** — proper async pattern, clear assertion

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| **1** | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, …)` to `BulkInsert` | ~2 min |
| **2** | Conditional Test Logic | Split `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` into 2 tests | ~10 min |
| **3** | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll loop + timeout | ~10 min |
